  "worked_solution": "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that we are given the set $∅.$ So, its power set must be $\\{∅\\}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set $\\{a,∅\\}.$ So, its power set must be $\\{∅,\\{a\\},\\{∅\\},\\{a,∅\\}\\}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the power set of the set $\\{∅\\}$ is $\\{∅,\\{∅\\}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
